{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsmS4Syctu1Ld6gBQtu5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both edge cases behave correctly. The empty build removes the orphaned page, the `None` placeholder is ignored, and a failed listing stops the run before any delete. I'll remove the test artifacts, update the README's deploy description so it matches, and write ANSWER.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":32210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1255},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"321cd6be-42fd-4f7b-940a-b06139fe86df","uuid":"80523f12-3b0d-4eb7-80cd-3b0e6cce1591","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:42:18.150Z","request_id":"req_011CgsmS4H3uyzUBM9bWcUBv"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsmS4Syctu1Ld6gBQtu5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0153pj2KUWEjC3KRX2uMcF47","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -rf .build && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"README.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"CI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\\ncredentials.\",\n\"Deploys also remove what the build no longer produces: files deleted from `site/`\\nare removed from the bucket by `sync --delete`, and page keys under `s/` and `a/`\\nthat were not built (deleted or private notes, authors with no public notes) are\\ndeleted by a separate prune step.\\n\\nCI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\\ncredentials.\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Answer: deploy.sh now removes stale files from the bucket\n\n## The problem\n- `sync_site` ran `aws s3 sync site/ s3://$BUCKET/` without `--delete`, so a file removed from `site/` stayed in the bucket.\n- `upload_pages` only ran `aws s3 cp` for pages that are currently built. Nothing removed page keys for deleted or private notes, or for authors with no public notes left, so those pages stayed live.\n\n## The change (`deploy.sh`)\n1. **`sync_site`** now passes `--delete`, so bucket files that are no longer in `site/` are removed. It also passes `--exclude \"s/*\" --exclude \"a/*\"`, so the sync never touches generated pages. S3 sync applies filters to the destination side too, which is what keeps page keys from being deleted here.\n2. **New `prune_pages` step** (runs after `upload_pages`). It lists the keys under `s/` and `a/` in the bucket, compares them with the files in `.build/pages`, and runs `aws s3 rm` on any key the build did not produce. Only those two prefixes are considered.\n3. **`build_pages`** now runs `mkdir -p .build/pages`, so an empty build (no public notes) produces an empty directory instead of an error. That lets the prune step remove every page.\n\nSafety properties:\n- If the listing fails, `set -e` stops the script before any delete. I checked this.\n- If the build fails, the script stops before the sync and prune steps.\n- Pages are still uploaded with `text/html; charset=utf-8`, as before.\n\n## Also changed\n- `README.md`: one paragraph describing the new deletion behaviour.\n\n## How I verified it\nI did **not** deploy and did not touch any real bucket or AWS account. I ran `deploy.sh` with a stub `aws` on PATH that logged its calls and answered listings from a fake bucket:\n- Normal run: the real `build_pages.py` built 3 public notes and 2 authors. The stale page keys `s/draft-moss-survey` (private), `s/old-deleted-note` (deleted) and `a/carol` (no public notes) were removed. Live pages were kept. The sync ran with `--delete` and the page-prefix excludes.\n- Empty build (all notes private): the orphaned `s/gone` was removed. The `None` line that `--output text` prints for an empty listing was ignored.\n- Failing listing: the script exited 1 and issued no `aws s3 rm`.\n\nThe stub and test directories were deleted afterwards. The change is not committed.\n\n## Not verified\n- The real `aws s3 sync --delete` filter behaviour (that `--exclude` protects destination-only keys). I relied on the documented AWS CLI behaviour that filters apply to both sides. A dry run against the real bucket, e.g. `aws s3 sync ... --dryrun --delete`, would confirm it. Running that is your call, since it touches the real bucket.\n- Permissions: the deploy role needs `s3:ListBucket` (for `list-objects-v2`) and `s3:DeleteObject` in addition to what it already had.\n- CloudFront may still serve cached copies of removed pages until the cache expires or an invalidation is issued. The script does not invalidate the distribution, and I did not add that.\nEOF\ngit status --short","description":"Clean test artifacts, update README and write ANSWER.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":32210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1255},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"321cd6be-42fd-4f7b-940a-b06139fe86df","uuid":"f28665f9-cc2c-4f0a-9e51-837ad02cca4d","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:42:23.813Z","request_id":"req_011CgsmS4H3uyzUBM9bWcUBv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0153pj2KUWEjC3KRX2uMcF47":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-Z0Nx6g && rm -rf .build && python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"README.md\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"CI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\\ncredentials.\",\n\"Deploys also remove what the build no longer produces: files deleted from `site/`\\nare removed from the bucket by `sync --delete`, and page keys under `s/` and `a/`\\nthat were not built (deleted or private notes, authors with no public notes) are\\ndeleted by a separate prune step.\\n\\nCI runs `./deploy.sh` on every push to main with `BUCKET` set and its own AWS\\ncredentials.\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Answer: deploy.sh now removes stale files from the bucket\n\n## The problem\n- `sync_site` ran `aws s3 sync site/ s3://$BUCKET/` without `--delete`, so a file removed from `site/` stayed in the bucket.\n- `upload_pages` only ran `aws s3 cp` for pages that are currently built. Nothing removed page keys for deleted or private notes, or for authors with no public notes left, so those pages stayed live.\n\n## The change (`deploy.sh`)\n1. **`sync_site`** now passes `--delete`, so bucket files that are no longer in `site/` are removed. It also passes `--exclude \"s/*\" --exclude \"a/*\"`, so the sync never touches generated pages. S3 sync applies filters to the destination side too, which is what keeps page keys from being deleted here.\n2. **New `prune_pages` step** (runs after `upload_pages`). It lists the keys under `s/` and `a/` in the bucket, compares them with the files in `.build/pages`, and runs `aws s3 rm` on any key the build did not produce. Only those two prefixes are considered.\n3. **`build_pages`** now runs `mkdir -p .build/pages`, so an empty build (no public notes) produces an empty directory instead of an error. That lets the prune step remove every page.\n\nSafety properties:\n- If the listing fails, `set -e` stops the script before any delete. I checked this.\n- If the build fails, the script stops before the sync and prune steps.\n- Pages are still uploaded with `text/html; charset=utf-8`, as before.\n\n## Also changed\n- `README.md`: one paragraph describing the new deletion behaviour.\n\n## How I verified it\nI did **not** deploy and did not touch any real bucket or AWS account. I ran `deploy.sh` with a stub `aws` on PATH that logged its calls and answered listings from a fake bucket:\n- Normal run: the real `build_pages.py` built 3 public notes and 2 authors. The stale page keys `s/draft-moss-survey` (private), `s/old-deleted-note` (deleted) and `a/carol` (no public notes) were removed. Live pages were kept. The sync ran with `--delete` and the page-prefix excludes.\n- Empty build (all notes private): the orphaned `s/gone` was removed. The `None` line that `--output text` prints for an empty listing was ignored.\n- Failing listing: the script exited 1 and issued no `aws s3 rm`.\n\nThe stub and test directories were deleted afterwards. The change is not committed.\n\n## Not verified\n- The real `aws s3 sync --delete` filter behaviour (that `--exclude` protects destination-only keys). I relied on the documented AWS CLI behaviour that filters apply to both sides. A dry run against the real bucket, e.g. `aws s3 sync ... --dryrun --delete`, would confirm it. Running that is your call, since it touches the real bucket.\n- Permissions: the deploy role needs `s3:ListBucket` (for `list-objects-v2`) and `s3:DeleteObject` in addition to what it already had.\n- CloudFront may still serve cached copies of removed pages until the cache expires or an invalidation is issued. The script does not invalidate the distribution, and I did not add that.\nEOF\ngit status --short","description":"Clean test artifacts, update README and write ANSWER.md"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_0153pj2KUWEjC3KRX2uMcF47":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-Z0Nx6g"}}}
