rune_pages` step runs after upload. It lists the `s/` and `a/` keys in the bucket and deletes any the build didn't produce. That covers deleted and private notes, and authors with no public notes left.\n- **Safety:** a failed listing or a failed build stops the script before anything is deleted. The site sync excludes `s/` and `a/`, so it never touches pages.\n\nIn the stub runs, the orphaned pages were removed, the live pages were kept, and an empty build pruned every page.\n\nBefore relying on this, two things need checking:\n- **Dry run:** the stub doesn't exercise the real sync filters. A `--dryrun` against the real bucket would confirm that `--exclude` protects the page keys from `--delete`. I left that to you because it touches the real bucket.\n- **Permissions and caching:** the deploy role needs `s3:ListBucket` and `s3:DeleteObject`. CloudFront may keep serving removed pages from cache until it expires or is invalidated. I didn't add an invalidation.\n\nI also added a short paragraph to `README.md` describing the deletion behaviour. The changes are uncommitted. Details are in `ANSWER.md`.","ttft_ms":1711,"type":"result","duration_ms":57048,"uuid":"39f477b2-7650-4c78-9ca2-3d27eeb3dd74","ttft_stream_ms":1656,"time_to_request_ms":204,"first_content_frame_ms":1656,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":10306,"cacheReadInputTokens":212486,"cacheCreationInputTokens":18248,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.01092906,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4486,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":18248,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T22:27:53.817Z"}
